    {
      "id": "p0179-b010",
      "kind": "aside",
      "source": {
        "text": "In Japanese, sushi technically refers to a type of vinegared rice rather than raw fish, meaning there are genuine, authentic, non-fish types of sushi if you don't like fish (inari is my favorite!)",
