    {
      "id": "p0179-b012",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "At first, the translator changed \"smells like sushi\" to \"smells like a fish market\" and explained that Japanese players are more likely to associate the smell of sushi with vinegared rice rather than raw fish. Much later, Toby noted that \"smells like sushi\" is a fan-favorite quote and asked that it be reinstated in Japanese.",
        "raw": "At first, the translator changed\n\"smells like sushi\" to \"smells like a fish\nmarket\" and explained that Japanese\nplayers are more likely to associate\nthe smell of sushi with vinegared rice\nrather than raw fish. Much later, Toby\nnoted that \"smells like sushi\" is a\nfan-favorite quote and asked that it be\nreinstated in Japanese.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.08242149,
          0.7498,
          0.38303799,
          0.91057857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
